  "query_preview": "..\nThe monsoon trough with imbedded Invest 92W to the southwest of the \nMarianas continues to push occasionally scattered showers into the \nregion along with increasingly southerly winds. This disturbance is \nexpected to keep its distance and keep the Marianas dry overall for \nthe next few days, with the exception of increasing island effect \nshowers and thunderstorms. Guam may receive slightly more rainfall \ndue to its closer proximity to 92W. Light to gentle winds will slowly\ndrop off to light and variable winds tomorrow night. This will allow\nisland effect showers and thunderstorms to develop in the afternoon \nthrough Saturday for Guam, Tinian, and Saipan. Winds may even be \nlight enough Thursday for Rota to recieve island effect showers. \nCoverage will depend on how clear conditions are in the mornings. As\na shearline/cold front and the band of convergence near Chuuk\ninteract, this may increase the chance for precipitation over the \nMarianas Wednesday night. However, this remains uncertain so isolated\nshowers and thunderstorms remain in the forecast. Afterwards, \noverall shower coverage is expected to return to isolated over the \nweekend, with isolated thunderstorms returning at the end of the week\nas Invest 93W potentially approaches the Marianas.",
